 ## inspect
 
 `/context` shows the prepared request: its sections in order, their sources, and compaction status. After a provider completes that request, it shows the provider's measured input tokens (and cached tokens when reported); until then, or when usage is omitted, the strategy's local estimate is shown instead. The JSON retains `estimated_input_tokens` separately from `provider_input_tokens` so neither is mistaken for the other. A manual `/compact` sends no ordinary provider request, so its snapshot has only an estimate. See [the context inspector](context.md).
+
+## Settings captured per preparation
+
+A strategy resolves once to `Resolved(capacity, project, compact)` before request
+context capture. Its closures retain validated settings across project, compact
+and project. Genuine capacity preserves each strategy's precedence: rolling and
+LCM configuration before catalog; visual snapcompact catalog before its setting;
+text-only snapcompact captures rolling settings once. A forced synthetic window
+remains internal to compaction and is unknown to contributors/inspection.
+
+Rendered mandatory dynamic blocks are reserved with static instructions and
+tools; they are not inserted into raw history. Optional blocks cannot force
+history eviction or an indivisible-tail refusal: final admission gives them the
+space remaining after projected history. Initial impossible optionals are
+omitted whole from the end, leaving mandatory history allowance. After pin settlement
+the host prices the actual assembled request with the existing local estimator,
+removes further optional blocks whole, and refuses mandatory overflow before
+foreground provider entry, including a request with no dynamic blocks. A stock
+summary call may already have occurred when overflow is only knowable after
+compaction releases a pin; initially provable overflow makes no summary call.
