+
+## Captured request context
+
+`RequestContextPlugin(prepare, required)` contributes bounded read-only native
+context once per actual request preparation. It receives the store/session, fully
+active bundle names, a recent user/steering query capped at 4096 UTF-8 bytes, and
+the genuine remaining window after static instructions and tool schemas. This is
+a trusted native semantic contract, not a security sandbox. The extension owns
+its coherent source revision and returns an opaque snapshot ID, whole mandatory
+or optional instruction/data blocks and diagnostics. Identity and memory policy
+do not belong to the host interface.
+
+The composition collects callbacks only from complete active bundles. A required
+requested bundle that failed loading refuses preparation. Any active callback
+error or exception stops preparation. Admission and capability inspection do not
+invoke callbacks. Dynamic data is never durable history or raw compaction input.
